# gh #51 (docs/20 U26), the user's ask: G0 twice starts a hands-free memo on the second
# press (no words lost); letting go ends nothing; the page says so plainly while Mando
# listens; one G0 press ends it, saved. A single tap still opens the note, once the 0.35 s
# double-tap window ran out. Locked, it goes on; G0 on the lit card ends it and the card
# says it was saved. The 5-minute cap ends a hands-free memo too. docs/20 D5: ` leaves the
# note (Fn+` would type a backtick into it).
# After the review: a slow second tap (to 1 s) still starts it and closes the empty note;
# a slow tap-then-hold records; tapping twice to end opens nothing; Tab, Enter does not end
# it; the menu's row starts one that ends at the cap with nothing held.
boot store=sd usb=on bat=4100 lang=zh
include ../common/demo_state.cpas
wait 1000
press g0
shot note  Tap G0: no second tap within 0.35 s, Note opens
press `
wait 600
press g0
press g0
mic 3000 speech
shot handsfree  G0 x2: hands-free, on after let go; Mando listens; hint [G0]stop [1-9]project [Opt+L]lock, 0 in legend
press 2
mic 1500 speech
shot handsfree-tag  2 while hands-free: saves to project 2, the recording goes on
press tab
shot handsfree-menu  Tab menu, hands-free: G0 Stop and save (a note only), 0-9, Opt+L
press enter
mic 300 speech
shot handsfree-menu-enter  Tab, then Enter: does not end; "Tap G0 to stop and save"
press tab
mic 800 speech
press g0
wait 300
shot handsfree-saved  G0 once more: ends, "Recording saved"
wait 2600
# tapping twice to end, as it started: the second tap opens nothing
press g0
press g0
mic 2000 speech
press g0
press g0
wait 600
shot end-double  Two taps to end: saved, the second opens no Note
wait 2600
# a slow double tap (the second press 0.5 s after the first): the note opens, then closes
press g0
wait 470
shot slow-note  0.35 s after the first tap: Note is open
press g0
mic 1500 speech
shot slow-handsfree  Second tap at 0.5 s: Note closes, hands-free starts
press g0
wait 2600
# tap, then hold: an ordinary held memo (the hold started it, no words lost)
press g0
down g0
wait 800
mic 1500 speech
shot tap-then-hold  Tap, then hold: an ordinary held memo
up g0
wait 900
wait 2600
# a slow tap-then-hold (the hold 1.2 s after the tap): the empty note closes, a held memo
press g0
wait 1170
down g0
wait 600
mic 1500 speech
shot slow-hold  Tap, hold 1.2 s later: the empty Note closes, an ordinary held memo
up g0
wait 900
wait 2600
# locked: it goes on; G0 from dark only lights the card; on the lit card it ends and says so
press g0
press g0
mic 1500 speech
press opt+l
mic 4000 speech
shot locked  Opt+L hands-free: locked, the recording goes on
press g0
mic 300 speech
shot locked-card  Locked, tap G0: card lit only, "Hands-free: [G0]ends it"
press g0
wait 300
shot locked-ended  G0 on the lit card: ends, the card says "√ Saved", Mando "Saved" (docs/20 B1), still locked
wait 2200
shot locked-still  After the end the card stays lit (3 s from that press)
wait 1500
shot locked-dark  Dark after 3 s
press g0
shot locked-again  Lit again: result seen, back to "Tap [G0]then hold · 2 taps: hands-free"
press opt+l
press enter
wait 2600
# the menu's row "G0 x2 Hands-free memo", then the 5-minute cap: saved, nothing held
press tab
press right
press down down down down down down down
shot menu-row  Tab → Go: G0 x2 Hands-free memo
press enter
mic 290000 2500
shot cap-4m50  Hands-free 4:50 (started from the menu)
mic 12000 2500
shot cap  5:00 auto stop: 5 min limit reached · saved, no "Let go of [G0]"
press tab
shot cap-tab  Tab works at once
press tab
wait 2600
